Annualized time-weighted return uses the first and last investor flow dates.
The requested interval starts a year before the first purchase and ends eleven
months after the complete sale. Those empty edges do not extend the return
period. A 100 USD fund purchase on January 1 becomes 110 USD on February 1;
the total return is 10% over 31 days and the annualized return is
(1.10)^(365 / 31) - 1 = 207.16%.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts '*Assets:Fund*' --from 2022-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Gains
P 2023-01-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2023-02-01 FUND 110 USD

2023-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

2023-02-01 Complete sale
  Assets:Fund  -1 FUND {100 USD} @ 110 USD
  Assets:Cash  110 USD
  Income:Gains  -10 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2022-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: -10.00 USD
Ending value: 0.00 USD
Profit/loss: 10.00 USD
Time-weighted return (total): 10.00 %
Time-weighted return (annualized): 207.16 %
Money-weighted return (total): 10.00 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 207.16 %

